<%#
  One field-level error message.

  Error codes come from the validation layer (zod messages, or the reason
  strings the query modules return) and are translated here, so no message
  text is built in JavaScript.

  A code with its own `error.field.<code>` entry gets that specific message;
  anything else falls back to a generic one. Existence is checked rather than
  matched against a list in this file — such a list fell behind as new codes
  were added, and the affected fields quietly showed "invalid value" instead
  of the real reason.

  Expects `code` and `hasT`.
-%>
<% if (code) { %>
  <span class="field__error">
    <%= hasT('error.field.' + code) ? t('error.field.' + code) : t('error.field.generic') %>
  </span>
<% } %>
